WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.000
Hey Wisecrack, Jared here.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:10.889
Today, we’re looking at another offering
from the mind of ONE, the Japanese manga artist

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:13.540
behind one of our favorite shows, One Punch
Man.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.849
I’m talking, of course, about the hilarious
and thought-provoking Mob Psycho 100.

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:23.360
Like One Punch Man, Mob Psycho 100 explores
what it means to live a fulfilling life by

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.410
unpacking the unique challenges faced by an
overpowered protagonist.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:32.550
Unlike Saitama, however, Shigeo Kageyama finds
a way to make peace with his abilities and

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.899
get satisfaction out of life in spite of them.

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:36.899
How does he do it?

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:38.320
Well, let’s dig in and find out.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.710
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on the Philosophy
of Mob Psycho 100.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.500
And spoilers ahead, for mostly season one
since season two is still in progress.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.700
Now first, a quick recap.Our main character,
Mob, is a middle schooler born with psychic

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.850
powers that give him a near-godlike ability
to manipulate the world around him.The young

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.590
psychic spends his afternoons working for
Reigen Arataka, a con man masquerading as

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.989
a powerful psychic.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.549
From the beginning of their time together,
Reigen tells Mob that he must never use his

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:08.340
powers against another human being.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.150
“However, if you misuse a power that's all
too great, you'll only destroy yourself.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:18.650
That's why I'm teaching you how to control
your powers, so they don't go berserk.”

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:22.729
So Mob spends his days trying to live the
life of a normal middle-schooler,repressing

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:27.759
the rage that fuels his powers which, in spite
of his best efforts, occasionally gets away

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:28.759
from him.

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:32.630
When other superpowered humans - called ‘espers’
- attack Mob and his friends,

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.770
he is torn between the desire to defend his
loved ones and his promise not to hurt other

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:38.770
people.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.869
Mob’s reluctance to use his powers might
seem a little weird.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:44.889
At first glance, having psychic powers seems
like a sweet deal.

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:49.310
Teru, the ‘shadow leader’ of the gang
from a rival Middle School, uses his powers

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.840
to bully his schoolmates into submission.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.920
As a result, he seems to have everything a
teenage boy could want: Attention, respect,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.279
power, etc.

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:00.819
In other words all things Mob lacks.

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:04.819
Dimple, the power-hungry ghost who becomes
Mob’s sidekick after a failed attempt to

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:06.390
possess him,puts it pretty bluntly:

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.510
“He's put his psychic powers to good life
and live a fulfilling life.”

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:16.200
With the exception of Mob,the espers and other
powerful beings of this world are profoundly

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.610
egocentric,viewing themselves as the “main
characters” of an unfolding story rather

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.680
than regular people with limitations.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.939
“After all, I’m the main character of
this world.”

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:30.519
But Mob doesn’t want the superficially perfect
life of Teru.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:33.970
He’d prefer to earn his more fulfilling
existence.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:39.209
Mob believes that an easy life built entirely
around his innate gifts would be “pointless,”

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:42.680
because the things he wants are things he’ll
have to work for:

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:48.590
"Are there things you can't have even if you
use your powers?"

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:50.069
"Not at all!

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.540
You can even become god!"

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.500
"Muscles"
"What is he talking about?"

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.150
"Or the ability to understand girls, or read
my suroundings.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.060
I think there's even more than that"

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.940
Taking a cue from his master Reigen, Mob argues
that accepting or realizing limitations can

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.879
have a positive influence on one’s life.

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:12.299
And he has an ally in Irish philosopher Edmund
Burke.

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:16.660
Burke is most well-known for his description
of “the sublime,” the feeling of experiencing

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:21.400
oneself as infinitesimally small in the face
of vast forces beyond one’s control.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:27.000
To put it another way: the sublime, according
to Burke, is that which suspends or even destroys

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.049
egocentricity through a display of power or
grandeur that completely overwhelms one’s

00:03:32.049 --> 00:03:33.049
own capabilities.

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:36.700
It’s the feeling you might get looking at
a mountain range, staring into deep space,

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.269
or sailing a ship through a thunderstorm.

00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:43.090
Robert J. Oppenheimer might have been feeling
the sublime when he tested the first nuclear

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.090
weapons in the Nevada desert.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.349
You get the idea.

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:50.549
Burke believed that such experiences were
a vital part of a healthy life, in that they

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:55.660
force us to use mental and spiritual capacities
we might otherwise prefer to ignore—namely

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.930
those which remind us we are not at the center
of the universe.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:04.249
According to Burke, a life spent avoiding
the challenging scenarios that make the experience

00:04:04.249 --> 00:04:08.790
of the sublime possible can get very unhealthy,
very quickly.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.581
He held that the experience of the sublime,
in a literal way, exercises parts of our minds

00:04:13.581 --> 00:04:18.720
and bodies which rarely get activated in day-to-day
life, but which are vital to our wellbeing-

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.910
specifically, the parts which “tense up”
in response to fear.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.910
As he puts it:

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.880
“Labour [is] a thing absolutely requisite
to make us pass our lives with tolerable satisfaction

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.480
[...] Melancholy, dejection, despair, and
often self-murder, is the consequence of the

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.460
gloomy view we take of things in this relaxed
state of body.”

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.980
In other words, getting too “relaxed”
about one’s place in the universe is a quick

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.280
way to majorly bum yourself out.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.270
This is exactly the trap that the majority
of the show’s espers have fallen into.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:51.950
Like the Paradisers in One Punch Man, Teru
and the leaders of Claw carry around a massive

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:56.780
sense of entitlement which, far from bringing
them what they need to be truly happy, instead

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.820
leaves them feeling miserable when the real
world fails to give them what they falsely

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.860
believe they deserve:

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:06.540
“It’s hard to live...surviving’s a chore,
even though I’m so special.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:13.130
It’s obvious I’m amazing, why won’t
you just acknowledge that?

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.560
I’m a gift!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.940
This planet should put me on a pedestal and
worship me!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:16.940
That is the only world that is worthy of me.”

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.120
Mob recognizes early on that these espers
have no substance to their being:

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.820
“If you take away your psychic powers, there’ll
be nothing left.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:24.820
You’ll be empty.”

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.770
Because the espers are dependent on their
powers for their sense of identity and worth,

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.630
they can’t tolerate any attacks on their
constructed self-image.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:37.180
“If I let you infiltrate the facility like
this, my reputation will be ruined!”

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:41.431
Teru displays this fragility towards the end
of his fight with Mob.Frustrated with Mob

00:05:41.431 --> 00:05:44.970
for not fighting back, Teru breaks down and
tells him:

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:54.100
“As long as I used my powers, everything
went just the way I wanted…”

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.510
“What was that shot?

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:56.570
That was amazing!”

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.340
“We’re sorry please forgive us.”

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.470
“And yet,you took my world…”
“u-um…

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:03.300
I made some cookies if you’d like some.”

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.300
“You…

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.300
Your existence… destroyed that”

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.770
Teru perceives Mob’s refusal to fight as
a “rejection” of him - not just an annoyance

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:16.160
or an insult,but a direct assault on his self-perception
as an opponent worthy of Mob’s full strength.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.490
Teru can’t stand Mob’s patronizing because
it denies his self-perception;

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.950
and as Mob points out, Teru has nothing without
that.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.950
“Oh.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:25.950
I just realized why you hold such animosity
toward me.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.680
You don't like me because we're the same.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.230
You're sort of like me Hanazawa...

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:37.890
Not the fact that we both have psychic powers,
but the fact that you have no confidence in

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.600
yourself, just like me”

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.370
Like Saitama’s strength, the espers’ abilities
are a double-edged sword.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:47.980
Left unchecked, they make it easy for to believe
that they are inherently better than other

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:52.620
humans,and therefore are deserving of special
treatment:Now this way of thinking leaves

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:58.120
them feeling deeply unsatisfied, no matter
how much power or status they attain.What

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:03.010
these espers need is a reality check, a reminder
that they are subject to the same set of rules

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:06.960
as the rest of the human race:in other words,
they need to have their egos brought down

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.750
a peg by an overwhelming experience with the
sublime.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:15.710
Burke described the experience as a terrifying
but ultimately pleasant feeling resulting

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.550
from the healthy exercise of mind, body, and
spirit.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:24.330
A mind that never experiences its own insignificance
is therefore a weak mind.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:29.350
In the same way that a body gets weak without
exercise, that weakness is what allows “Melancholy,

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.890
dejection, despair,” and all that other
fun stuff to take root in the first place.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.930
He claims that:

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:40.480
“The best remedy for all these evils is
to exercise or labour; and labour is a surmounting

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.480
of difficulties[.]

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:46.600
[For mind and body to work] in proper order,
they must be shaken and worked to a proper

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.830
degree.”

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:52.280
Unlike the deluded espers, Mob wants to do
the difficult “labour” of integrating

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.830
himself into the world and society,rather
than trying to transcend it.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.940
So he finds some friends to help him do just
that.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:00.980
“FIGHT ON!

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.020
FIGHT ON!

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.060
FIGHT ON!”

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:07.690
Like Burke, Musashi Gouda and the other members
of the Body Improvement Club view “surmounting

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.970
of difficulties” as the key to a fulfilling
life.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:16.140
Unlike Teru, Dimple, and the Section 7 Division
Leader,they choose to challenge those parts

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.200
of themselves which are weakest,rather than
rely on their innate strengths and let the

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.410
rest of their bodies and minds waste away.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.010
“Remember the pain and how good it feels
Onigawara”

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:30.720
The espers, on the other hand, avoid “difficulties”
by relying on their psychic powers to gain

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.740
social status and uphold a false sense of
self-worth.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:39.090
As such, they have to be “shaken and worked”
by forces outside their control before they

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.710
can find a true sense of fulfillment.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:46.680
Teru is the clearest example.When Mob defeats
him, Teru is overwhelmed by his power and

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:52.140
feels terror, the emotion Burke identifies
as a key component of the experience of the

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.900
sublime.For the first time in his life, Teru
feels utter helplessness and the fear of death

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:01.930
as he is shorn of his hair stripped naked,and
hoisted up into the sky by Mob’s runaway

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.200
psychic powers.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.730
“That’s enough, I’m sorry!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:11.420
I won’t use my psychic powers against other
people!!”

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:15.640
After pleading for Mob to stop, Teru gets
cast into the sky and the chaos gives way

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:20.500
to a serene moment of reflection, where he’s
dwarfed by the clouds and an endless vista

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:21.950
in the background.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:26.180
Such visuals are reminiscent of classical
Romantic art, which was influenced by Burke’s

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:31.870
ideas and often portrayed small human subjects
facing vast, overwhelming forces of nature.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:36.060
The realization that he is not nearly the
most powerful being in the universe brings

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.670
Teru real peace.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.670
“Oh.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:42.980
I guess...I’m just an average person after
all…”

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.760
In a subtler way, Reigen exposes the remaining
“Scars” to the sublime by crushing their

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.150
delusions of grandeur through a combination
of Mob’s transferred powers and his own

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.150
rhetoric.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:57.630
He puts things in perspective by reminding
the Scars that, even with their powers, they’re

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.630
not special.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.630
"Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.850
You're nothing more than a commoner.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:04.670
You're just part of the masses."

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:11.000
"b-but claw is a noble --"
"I'm a commoner I'm much more powerful than

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.430
you, and I'm still just a commoner.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:18.360
So what does that make you?"

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:25.760
He dragged them out of their delusions and
back into reality by force.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:30.950
Like Mob does for Teru, Reigen shows the Scars
proof of their utter insignificance, giving

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:35.090
them a taste of the sublime and putting them
on the path toward a healthier, more grown-up

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.210
state of mind.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:42.070
For the espers, the key to freedom is realizing
that they are still human, small and vulnerable

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.620
as the rest of us.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.440
As the show’s theme song puts it:

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:51.210
“If everyone is not special” “Maybe
you can be what you want to be…”

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:55.430
Which is all well and good when you’re an
average esper like Teru or the Scars.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:59.560
But how do you experience the sublime when
you really are the closest thing to a god

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.470
that anyone has ever seen?

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.270
That is, how is Mob going to get back in touch
with reality?

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:09.770
Mob has a leg up on the other espers in that
he actually wants to be a normal person.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.910
He tries to improve his physical abilities
and social skills by joining the Body Improvement

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:18.900
Club, and he repeatedly states his admiration
for his brother Ritsu, who accomplishes so

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:22.330
much even before he discovers his own psychic
powers.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.960
"What can your little brother do."

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.300
"He's really smart.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:32.870
Unlike me who can't do anything without psychic
powers he can figure anything out and solve

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:33.870
any problem."

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:35.000
But Mob can’t get there on his own.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.790
Like the other espers, he is plagued by a
delusional self-image, albeit a less dickish

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.790
one.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.270
As a 14-year-old kid, Mob is under the delusion
that he has to be in total control of his

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:51.310
world at all times that he is profoundly responsible
for everything that happens during his unconscious

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:56.760
psychic episodes.This causes him to repress
his emotions out of fear that he will be overwhelmed

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:57.760
by his rage.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.480
“There are times when my psychic power goes
out of control…

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.670
“And it happens when I’m unconscious,
to boot”

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:07.430
Ironically, this gives him even less control
over when and how he explodes.The weight of

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:11.120
this responsibility is incredibly painful
for him:

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:17.680
“He failed to change as he had promised
himself...he caused another accident.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:22.520
He didn’t know where to direct his emotions.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:27.310
He was overwhelemd, his powerlessness born
from contradictions.”

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:34.680
“The feeling that he would never be able
to conquer himself…”

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.680
“sadness…”

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:41.370
“This was Mob’s meager attempt at resistance
towards himself.”

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:45.990
In other words, while Mob talks a big game
about wanting to be normal, in reality he

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.960
clings to an image of himself as the main
mover and shaker of his world, responsible

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:56.150
for everything that happens in it:this is
his delusion, a more benevolent version of

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.570
the other espers’ greedy desire for godhood.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:02.210
“I realized I have to do it to protect everyone”

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:06.460
It takes Reigen, an adult Mob respects and
looks up to, to remind him that he is just

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:10.470
a kid, and that he doesn’t always have to
bear the world on his shoulders:

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.900
“Don’t do it, Mob.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:18.980
In the end you’re the one who’s gonna
be suffering.”

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:24.450
“When things go south, it’s okay to run
away”

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.620
The idea that he doesn’t have to be at the
center of the fight after all shocks Mob into

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.210
an experience of the sublime Burke would say
he’d been properly “astonished”.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:39.160
It allows him to feel his own insignificance
and temporarily transfer his powers to Reigen.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:43.160
In this way, he is finally able to come to
terms with his abilities, and get on with

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:46.010
the business of living a good life.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:49.490
Which as we see in season two, comes with
it’s own struggles.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.180
No such luck for One Punch Man.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.240
Sorry, Saitama.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.420
“Back to one punch man again…”

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:59.920
We’ve had the chance to review two of ONE’s
biggest projects, and have started to notice

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.339
some interesting overlapping themes.

00:14:02.339 --> 00:14:07.620
Both One Punch Man and Mob Psycho 100 ask
us to really think about what constitutes

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.620
a good life.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:13.310
Saitama and Mob’s struggles with their powers
reveal that a fulfilling existence might not

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:17.110
be as simple as getting whatever you want
whenever you want it.

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:22.240
In the ONE-iverse, happiness is the result
of deliberate struggle and growth.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.450
